  ],
  "text": "In thirty years, one lizard population evolved an entirely new gut structure. Evolution is meant to be too slow to watch. That is the whole assumption. But it is not slow by nature. It is slow when nothing is pushing. Push hard enough and it moves fast. Ten lizards, one island, thirty years. Industrial soot turned the moths black in fifty years. Clean air turned them back. Under heavy poaching, more and more elephants are born with no tusks at all. And the fastest example we have is happening in hospitals, right now. Kill ninety nine percent of the bacteria and you have just chosen the other one percent. Evolution is not history. It is a process you are standing inside. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
